**Finding: Compliant** — no redline proposed.

The agreement contains no non-solicitation, no-hire, or anti-poaching covenant. Targeted searches for "solicit", "induce", "recruit", "hire" and "employ" surfaced only:

- **p0066** — independent contractor / no employment relationship boilerplate;
- **p0051 / p0052** — indemnity language referring to third parties "hired by, employed, retained or under [a party's] control";
- **p0056 / p0061** — confidentiality provisions permitting disclosure to employees and directors.

None of these impose a restriction on AP's ability to solicit, hire, or engage Kubient personnel. This matches our preferred position (no non-solicit on the Customer), so no fallback narrowing (12-month term, services-personnel scope, general-advertising carve-out) is needed. Worth monitoring only if Kubient introduces personnel or hiring restrictions in a later turn of the draft.
